From ac63bfc196e5deed9ac0329460caf370da1ecbbb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:26:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: a completion replayed before origin_gateway
 was recorded binds its leased run's receipt

Hub cards t_01a1ca1975471ed4, t_01a1cda0087499e3, t_01a1ce14309bff2c, t_01a1cf477dece56b, t_01a1cf6b6dd5feb4,
t_01a1cf7adf592a71, t_01a1d0622df6ea87 and t_01a1d087f0697ede ran on worker-2..6 on 2026-11-12. All are done
on the hub. On the hub, though, `read_completions(...).verified` is False for each, and chat
20261026_170127_f07c32 on laptop-1 lists them `unknown` (released=False). This is the same class as #2312: the
replayed `completed` payload carries the worker's local `pr_acceptance_event_id`. On the hub that id names
another card's event (3 of 8) or no event (5 of 8). These rows were replayed before the hub recorded
`task_events.origin_gateway`, which starts at event 1180961, so the completion and its receipts all have NULL
there. `pick` only takes #2312's same-run fallback when `imported_from` is set, so they stayed fail-closed.

Five whys:
1. Why `unknown`? The hub publishes verified=false, so the origin ledger never releases the card.
2. Why unverified? `pick` finds no receipt: the payload integer is worker-local.
3. Why no same-run fallback? It runs only for a completion with `origin_gateway` set.
4. Why is it NULL? The hub recorded replayed origins only from event 1180961; these were replayed earlier.
5. Why can't that be inferred? Nothing read the other proof the hub already holds: the Board's lease of the
   completing run (`claimed {holder: worker-N, run_uid}`, run_uid == task_runs.uid), which names the gateway
   that ran it.

Fix: `kanban_completion_refs.leased_elsewhere` (one SELECT per batch) returns, for each NULL-origin
completion, the single gateway other than this board's own (`kanban_sync_state.gateway_id`) that the Board
leased the completing run to. Such a completion is passed to `pick` as `imported_from=<holder>, legacy=True`.
Its receipts were replayed in the same pre-origin era, so they are matched on NULL origin in the same run. Both
`read_completions` (batch) and `observe_owner_task` (via `import_kwargs`) use it. The completion stays exact,
with no fallback, when:
- the run was held by this gateway;
- the run has no Board lease (an unsynced board, or a worker-local run);
- the lease names another run's uid, or is a lease of another run;
- the holder is not a string;
- two gateways leased the same run;
- the board cannot name itself.
`test_a_local_completion_with_a_wrong_id_stays_unverified` stays green.

Proof:
- tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_completion_refs_sync.py adds a plain case and a contract_waived case
  (t_01a1ca1975471ed4's shape: a refused no_required_checks try, then a waiver, in one run). Both FAIL on main
  d8727a4b282 and pass here. Six exact-stays-exact cases and the ambiguity case pass on both.
- Twelve exact-anchor mutants over every new condition, run with sdlc-review mutants.py: all killed
  (run_id match, run_uid match, run uid present, str holder, single holder, holder != own, own known,
  legacy origin both ways, batch flag, batch lookup, single-card lookup). The run-uid-present mutant
  survived the first round and is killed by the added no-run-uid test.
- Every test file that imports the changed modules (20 files, 482 tests) passes.
- Replay over the hub's real rows, read-only (`mode=ro`), old vs new `read_completions` over every done or
  archived card:
  - kanban.db: 215 of 5745 flip unverified -> verified, 0 flip down, all 8 incident cards included.
    For all 215, the worker-written `claimed {lock: hermes-<host>:pid}` of the completing run matches the
    Board lease holder. All are PR-contract completions with no goal_mode, and the bound receipt is success
    (165), no_required_checks + waiver (48) or closed (2).
  - boards/hermes: 4 up. boards/runners: 2 up. sync-shadow default/bb/hermes: 616/167/7 up. All boards: 0 down.
